      "wholeGoalAndWholeDEENProfileRead": true,
      "sourceBoundary": "p28/31/32 provide reaction and macromolecule contexts, not full urethane mechanism, equivalence and water-side-reaction credit. The existing LK theory unit remains an explicit own extension.",
      "scientificReason": "Alcohol O attacks the electrophilic isocyanate carbon; formal addition/proton transfer gives urethane without water elimination. A concerted or catalysed proton-transfer representation is allowed. Functionality and conversion govern branching/networking. A full water-to-urea path consumes two NCO groups per H2O: 2 mmol H2O consumes 4 mmol NCO and releases 2 mmol CO2, not evidence of network quality.",
