      "label": "Sigma-complex mechanism, LK",
      "wholeGoalAndWholeDEENProfileRead": true,
      "sourceBoundary": "p30 eA first substitution supplies direct partial context. The whole electron-pair, charge, octet and proton-transfer profile remains own acquisition; no actual nitration is certified.",
      "scientificReason": "The attacked ring carbon becomes sp3; the sigma complex temporarily lacks cyclic aromatic delocalisation. Base-to-H and C–H-to-ring arrows restore aromaticity. For nitronium attack a N=O pair shifts to O so nitrogen retains an octet; ring deprotonation transfers H+, not hydride. The stated net charge balances are coherent.",
